Package: omnihear
Version: 1.0.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-tk, portaudio19-dev, libx11-6, libxtst6, libxi6
Recommends: libnotify-bin, xdotool, ydotool
Suggests: wtype
Maintainer: dsb <you@example.com>
Description: Push-to-talk local Whisper transcription for Linux
 omnihear lets you hold a hotkey to record audio and have it
 transcribed locally via faster-whisper (no cloud, no network calls
 during use), then typed directly into whichever field has focus.
 .
 Works on X11 and Wayland. On Wayland, add your user to the `input`
 group for hotkeys (`sudo usermod -aG input $USER`, then re-login)
 and install ydotool (any compositor) or wtype (wlroots). Run
 `omnihear --help` for CLI options.
